# Hotel PMS UI

Follow **`docs/UI_PLAYBOOK_SATELLITES.md`** and existing hotel patterns (`GuestCardModal`, reservation cards, ElektraWeb-era layouts).

- Use `@era/satellite-kit/ui` primitives where available (`MODAL_INPUT_CLASS`, etc.).
- List grids: `HotelDataGrid` (wraps kit `EraDataGrid` with i18n `ListPaginationFooter`) — not bare `EraDataGrid`.
- Guest identity: support AZ FIN and foreign passport (`GuestCardIdentityTab`).
- If UX conflicts with playbook, follow playbook or ask the user.

## List screens (required)

- Every table/grid page: `PageHeader` -> `EraListFilterBar` (Field*/DatePicker) -> `HotelDataGrid` (or shell+scroll table).
- **Class A (guests, FO reservations):** `LIST_PAGE_SHELL_CLASS` + `EraListWorkspace` + server `{ items, total, page, pageSize }` (25/50/100). Filters go in the query string — not client-only over a dump. Reservations default status filter = **Live** (`OPTION|CONFIRMED|IN_HOUSE`); All is explicit.
- **Class B (catalogs / modals):** client footer on by default (25/50/100); pass `pagination={false}` or `embedded` only for tiny modal lists.
- Table chrome: `DATA_TABLE_SHELL_CLASS` + `DATA_TABLE_SCROLL_CLASS` (or fill scroll inside workspace). Legacy `DATA_TABLE_VIEWPORT_CLASS` ok until migrated.
- CRUD add via modal (`ModalShell` + `Field*`), never `window.prompt`.
- Errors: `showApiError` toast — not inline `text-red-*` / StatusMessage for API failures.
- 3-tier tokens: `docs/adr/era-design-tokens-3tier.md` + `resolveField` / `columnFilters`.
- Guest CRM subpages: `GuestCrmPromptListPage` + `GuestCrmSubnav` layout under `/guests/[id]`.

## Modals (global kit rule)

- `ModalShell` / `EraModal`: backdrop does **not** close on click; no Esc dismiss. Exit only via Close / Cancel / footer buttons.
- While open: `document.body` scroll locked; overlay `pt-10` (not `pt-24`) so near-fullscreen cards fit without page scroll.
- FO cards use `MODAL_FULL_CLASS` (`max-h-[90vh]`).

## Reservation card (near-fullscreen modal)

- **Canon:** [docs/adr/hotel-reservation-card-and-party-ops.md](../../../docs/adr/hotel-reservation-card-and-party-ops.md) (Depart / Move / Swap landed as engineering API/SCREEN).
- **One source** for create and edit: `ReservationCardEditor` via `ReservationCardModal` (`reservationId` null = create). Same panels/tabs always; post-save actions disabled with `availableAfterSave` tooltip.
- One chrome only: `ModalShell` **title = guest name** (or new-reservation), **subtitle = status · short id**. Do **not** repeat identity above money strip.
- **Header snapshot**: Total / Deposit / Balance only; occupancy chip only for share / multi-room booking.
- Secondary actions → **icon** `headerActions` (Attach / Lightning / History / ⋮ Menu with Print+Lock). Save / Check-in → text `footer`. No duplicate Print button.
- Max width: `MODAL_FULL_CLASS` (~99vw / 1920px). Layout: **`lg:grid-cols-[3fr_7fr]`** (~30% left / 70% right).
- FO header actions: **Room booking** (single stay card) + **Group booking** (multi-stay wizard). Screen chain (RTA / list / rack / plan) stays in the sidebar, not as header chips.
- Left rail: Stay window (**row 1** date+time in + nights; **row 2** date+time out + one plane: red landing on CI day, red takeoff on CO day, yellow takeoff = IN_HOUSE early stay checkout) · Room (**Room type** = charge; **Given room type** = physical door list; when they differ, ask who pays — hotel covers, guest pays the given class, or a downgrade — do not call a cheaper given type a free upgrade; **Room no.** filters by Given else Room type; stable Lock/Search/HK/Assign; collapsed **Moves** under the room number, hidden when empty) · Pax & board (heads + meal; counters are the row age bands) · Rate & source (Source path + matching contract + rate) · Billing · Additional. No `roomCount` on single card.
- Right (~70%): tabs Guests · Pricing · Folio · Notes.
  - Guests: compact party grid only — **no** PRIMARY/EQUAL billing chrome; icon add/search/camera; VIP / trip reason on the specials strip.
  - Pricing: daily Rate Grid + quote preview + optional packageCompose summary.
  - Folio: All/Guest/Agency/Company; when party >1, **named guest sections** (not Opera windows).
  - Notes: NOTE_TYPE feed + FO/HK/Billing filters + add-type picker; open-card alert for CIN/EXTRA_REQ/allergens.
- StaysBar: **compact GRP strip** for 1 room; full family navigator only when sibling stays > 1.
- Create = edit same chrome; door assign / share block gated CONFIRMED+; **times always visible**.
- Tabs: kit `TAB_STRIP_CLASS` / `TAB_ITEM_*`; folio subtabs: `CHIP_*`.
- Stay dates: kit `DatePicker` + `common.datePlaceholder` (never native `type="date"` alone).
- Folio grid: `HotelDataGrid`. No raw hex buttons — `SUCCESS_BUTTON_CLASS` / `DANGER_BUTTON_CLASS` / `SECONDARY_BUTTON_CLASS` / `GHOST_BUTTON_CLASS` for icon headers.
- Front-cash **open folio** (balances, journal, cash transactions) opens `ReservationCardModal` on the Folio tab (`initialTab="folio"`), not the `/folio/[id]` page.

## Guest card (same FO chrome)

- **One source** for create and edit: `GuestCardModal` (`guestId` null = create). Same 50/50 + stats strip (zeros until saved) + left panels + right tabs.
- Same `MODAL_FULL_CLASS` + **50/50** grid. Stats strip above the split.
- Left: static `FieldPanel` groups — Identity (no phone/email, no composed full-name field) · Documents & MDM (read-only primary phone/email/document, visa, registration, MDM) · Commercial · Family · Other. Grey list and problematic are header chips. MDM lookup/merge stays in Documents. VÖEN is in Other, not next to a passport.
- Right tabs: Identity/Contact (the editor for contacts, documents, addresses, consents) · CRM · Reservations · Loyalty. **Time share is hidden** until a module flag exists (ADR hotel-reservation-card-and-party-ops). No separate Details tab.
- Chrome matches the reservation card: modal title = composed name, subtitle = short id, icon header (scanner, copy, menu → print + lock), Save in the footer. No inner text toolbar. Add document/contact/address/loyalty via `ModalShell`, never `window.prompt`. CRM tiles that belong to this guest open an in-card dialog.
- Dates via `DatePicker`; fields via kit `Field` / `FieldRow`.
- **Full name** is not a form field. The modal title is composed from first name + patronymic + last name on every change (`guestComposedFullName`). Legacy guests with only `fullName` get parts split on load. Create (`POST /api/guests`) persists the parts, title, sex, email and birth date, and passes them to the MDM link. Citizenship is ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 (legacy `OTHER` still accepted). Saving the card requires first name, last name, gender, birth date and citizenship (red asterisk). Phone and a travel document are not required until check-in; a guest under 18 does not need a phone.

## FO screen chain

Priority: **Room type availability** `/availability` → reservation list → rack `/` → room plan. See `docs/adr/hotel-fo-screen-chain.md`. Empty plan/rack cells = free doors, not sellable Avl.

## Room rack

- `/fo/rack`: From–To `DatePicker` interval (stay overlap); left filter column `overflow-y-auto` and room grid `overflow-y-auto` as separate panes (`LIST_PAGE_SHELL_CLASS`).

## Room plan

- Room plan (`/room-plan`): `EraListFilterBar` Tarix (`DatePicker` → API `from`) + Otaq/Qonaq client filters; grouping/period stay as `FilterMenuButton`; fullscreen overlay like clinic resource matrix (Esc exits). **Bar click / unassigned chip → reservation card** (not +1/+2 intercept modal). Drag-resize still extends checkout.
- Room plan bars (`room-plan/shapes.ts`): half-day (noon) model — box spans mid check-in column → mid check-out column. Right edge = blunt `arrow` (fixed `CHEVRON_PX`, not % of bar width) whenever checkout is in-window; `flat` only when clipped past the window. Left edge = matching EW butt notch for any in-window multi-night start; clipped start stays flat. Geometry is precomputed in `computePlacedBars`; `barSvgPath(flags, widthPx)` builds pixel user-space. Exclusive doors = single lane; share doors = N lanes via `share-lanes.ts` (never paint overlapping stays on the same `top`). Fill = day-state (`plan-bar-theme.ts`); **occupancy** = left badge (♂ blue / ♀ pink for **open** share pool; exclusive and **closed pair** have no badge). Stroke follows day-state. No HK squares on the plan — OOO/OOS/repair rooms omitted. Party companion names on the bar (primary omitted from `partyNames`); open-pool roommate names concatenated; closed pair = own name only. Guest folio debt badge on the arrow nose. Date header = large day + weekday (EW).
